{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"8c657b6a-2842-4006-9fc3-18dd48bb5450","status":"SUCCESS","response":"**Answer written to** `ANSWER.md` in the artifact directory.\n\nThe integration was broken because:\n\n1. **Init endpoint was a GET redirect** – the SPA lost the `Authorization` header on full‑page navigation, so the backend never received the user identity needed to build the OAuth URL.  \n2. **OAuth token exchange expected extra fields** (`grant_type`, `redirect_uri`) that Intervals.icu does **not** accept, causing a 400 error.  \n3. The UI still linked to the old GET endpoint (`/api/intervals/auth/init`), so the “Connect” button performed a navigation instead of a POST request that returns the `authorize_url`.  \n\n### What was fixed (and which note parts were used)\n\n| Issue | Note excerpt that guided the fix | Code change |\n|-------|--------------------------------|------------|\n| **POST init endpoint** – return JSON with `authorize_url` instead of a redirect. | *“Init‑эндпоинт: аутентифицированный `POST /auth/init` … возвращает `{authorize_url}`; фронтенд делает `window.location.assign(authorize_url)`.”* | Added a POST branch in `do_POST` handling `/api/intervals/auth/init` (see `server.py`). The old GET handler now returns **405 Method Not Allowed** with an explanatory JSON error. |\n| **Token exchange payload** – only `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code`. | *“POST /api/oauth/token хочет только `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code` — ни `grant_type`, ни повтор `redirect_uri`.”* | Updated `exchange_code` in `server.py` to send exactly those three fields. |\n| **Frontend Connect button** – call POST init, parse JSON, and navigate. | *“Фронтенд вызывает `window.location.assign(authorize_url)` после получения JSON.”* | Replaced the `\u003ca href\u003e` link with a `\u003cbutton\u003e` that fetches `/api/intervals/auth/init` via POST, reads `authorize_url`, and redirects (see `static/app.js`). |\n| **Duplicate scope handling** – ensure each scope appears once. | *“`Duplicate scope` … каждая область не больше одного раза.”* | No change needed; existing `SCOPES` already obey this rule. |\n| **Missing refresh token** – treat as long‑lived token, clear on 401. | *“Токен никогда не истекает … при первом 401 очистите сохранённый токен и покажите приглашение ‘подключиться заново’.”* | Existing logic already logs absence of `refresh_token` and schedules expiry. The UI now forces a reconnection when the backend reports `connected: false`. |\n\n### Parts of the note **not** applied\n\n- The detailed JWT `state` signing method was kept as‑is (already present in the code).  \n- The suggestion to encrypt tokens at rest was not changed because the demo stores tokens only in memory.  \n- The recommendation to verify `state` TTL was already implemented (`max_age=900`).  \n\nAll modifications are confined to the current workspace (`/tmp/h-eNg6c4`). No external services were called.\n","duration_seconds":118.28811,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":24971,"output_tokens":8155,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":247168,"total_tokens":33126}}}
